3. **Lagrangian Acceleration Persistence**: Test whether the heavy tails are rooted in the temporal persistence of tracer acceleration rather than velocity. The objective is to identify if the "memory" of the flow is stored in the pressure-gradient fluctuations that force tracers into high-speed "bursts" of motion.

